@page "/privacy"
@namespace Ben.Web.Website.Library.Support
@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<Ben.Data.Common.SiteIdentity> SiteOptions

@* Anonymous on purpose, and the reason is not only courtesy: App Store Connect requires a privacy
   policy URL that Apple's reviewer can open WITHOUT an account, and so does Google. A page behind
   a sign-in is a rejected submission. Nothing here reads the signed-in user — see
   feedback_author_sees_what_visitor_cannot for the class of bug that hides in pages like this. *@

<PageTitle>Privacy — @SiteOptions.Value.Name</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid px-3 py-4" style="max-width:860px; margin:auto;">

    <h1 class="mb-1">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary mb-4">
        How @SiteOptions.Value.Name and the IsHaunted iPhone and iPad app handle your information.
        Last updated 08/28/2026.
    </p>

    <div class="card border-primary mb-4">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h5 card-title mb-2">The short version</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                We collect nothing about you except what you give us directly. There is no
                advertising, no analytics or tracking service, no data broker, and nothing that
                follows you to other apps or websites. If you did not type it, upload it, or ask us
                to record it, we do not have it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What you give us</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Your account.</strong> An email address, a display name and an @@name. You may
            add a real name, a profile photo, a birth year and contact details — every one of those
            is optional and you control who can see it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>What you create.</strong> Cases, investigations, events, equipment records,
            notes, reports, messages, feed posts and comments — the substance of using the site.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Evidence you upload.</strong> Photos, video, audio and documents, together with
            whatever you write about them.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Field sessions from the app.</strong> Sensor readings, photos, audio and
            location, recorded on your device while a session is running.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Location, specifically</h2>
    <p>
        The app stamps readings with your location <em>only</em> while a field session is running,
        and only if you granted location permission. Those readings stay on your device unless you
        choose to upload the session to your group. Nothing tracks your location in the background,
        and the app never asks for always-on location.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We do not sell or rent your information, ever.</li>
        <li>We do not run advertising, and nothing here profiles you for anyone else's.</li>
        <li>We use no analytics, telemetry or crash-reporting service.</li>
        <li>We do not track you across other apps or websites.</li>
        <li>We do not buy information about you from anybody.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who else touches it</h2>
    <p>
        A short list, each for one job, and none of them receives anything for their own purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Apple and Microsoft</strong> — only if you choose Sign in with Apple or a Microsoft account. They tell us you signed in; we tell them nothing about you.</li>
        <li><strong>Our mail provider</strong> — to deliver the email the site sends you.</li>
        <li><strong>Geocod.io</strong> — turns an address you type into map coordinates. It receives the address, not your identity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see what you post</h2>
    <p>
        You decide, per item. Most things start private to you and the group you share them with.
        Cases marked as private engagements have client names and addresses hidden from everyone
        outside the group, including in anything published publicly. Anything you deliberately
        publish — a public case page, a feed post, a group profile — is public, which is the point
        of publishing it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
        For as long as your account exists. Delete an item and it goes; close your account and we
        remove your personal details and the content attached to you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Security</h2>
    <p>
        Traffic runs over HTTPS. Passwords are stored hashed and never in readable form, and you can
        turn on two-factor authentication in your account settings.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Children</h2>
    <p>
        @SiteOptions.Value.Name is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly
        collect information from them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Edit or delete what you have posted, at any time, from the item itself.</li>
        <li>Change what your profile shows other people in your account settings.</li>
        <li>Ask us for a copy of your information, or ask us to delete your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Asking us anything</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> — no account needed — for any question about
        this page, for a copy of your information, or to have your account removed.
    </p>

</div>
